{"3519900": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Cyberscape", "steam_appid": 3519900, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Cyberscape</strong> is a single-player FPS with RPG elements set entirely aboard a massive space station. Inspired by the deliberate pacing and mechanical depth of classic 90s shooters, the game focuses on exploration, character progression, and tactical combat within a single interconnected environment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The station is owned and controlled by a ruthless corporate Syndicate that treats people as expendable assets and ethics as optional expenses. Behind polished executive decks and carefully worded public statements, the Syndicate is pursuing projects that were never meant to withstand scrutiny.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Your objective is simple: infiltrate the station and put an end to it.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Multiple playable operatives</strong> - each with unique strengths, limitations, and playstyle implications</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Large hand-crafted levels</strong> - massive multi-level maps with multiple routes, hidden paths, unexpected dangers</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Skill progression</strong> - earn EXP and improve the abilities you actually rely on</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tactical combat</strong> - choose an appropriate tool for the job</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive elements</strong> - crawlspaces, keycard-gated areas, breakable walls, secret levels</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Varied enemy design</strong> - soldiers, mutants, drones, automated defenses, security cameras, experimental threats</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Meaningful replayability</strong> - different character builds unlock different playstyles</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Exploration</strong> - your map of the station is filled automatically as you explore</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Stealth mechanics</strong> - loud solutions tend to escalate things</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No hand-holding</strong> - the game respects your intelligence, like in the good old days</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Modding</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cyberscape ships with the same tools used to build the game.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Integrated level and scenario editor</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fully data-driven architecture for all game content</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Steam Workshop support from day one</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Support for everything from small balance tweaks to total conversions</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Modding is not an afterthought. It is part of the design.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About the Team</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cyberscape is developed by <strong>AtomicTorch Studio</strong>, an independent team with over a decade of experience building games on Steam. Known for CryoFall and VoidExpanse, the studio focuses on deep, open-ended mechanics, technical robustness, and long-term value and replayability.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Cyberscape</strong> is a single-player FPS with RPG elements set entirely aboard a massive space station. Inspired by the deliberate pacing and mechanical depth of classic 90s shooters, the game focuses on exploration, character progression, and tactical combat within a single interconnected environment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The station is owned and controlled by a ruthless corporate Syndicate that treats people as expendable assets and ethics as optional expenses. Behind polished executive decks and carefully worded public statements, the Syndicate is pursuing projects that were never meant to withstand scrutiny.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Your objective is simple: infiltrate the station and put an end to it.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Multiple playable operatives</strong> - each with unique strengths, limitations, and playstyle implications</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Large hand-crafted levels</strong> - massive multi-level maps with multiple routes, hidden paths, unexpected dangers</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Skill progression</strong> - earn EXP and improve the abilities you actually rely on</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tactical combat</strong> - choose an appropriate tool for the job</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive elements</strong> - crawlspaces, keycard-gated areas, breakable walls, secret levels</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Varied enemy design</strong> - soldiers, mutants, drones, automated defenses, security cameras, experimental threats</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Meaningful replayability</strong> - different character builds unlock different playstyles</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Exploration</strong> - your map of the station is filled automatically as you explore</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Stealth mechanics</strong> - loud solutions tend to escalate things</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No hand-holding</strong> - the game respects your intelligence, like in the good old days</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Modding</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cyberscape ships with the same tools used to build the game.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Integrated level and scenario editor</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fully data-driven architecture for all game content</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Steam Workshop support from day one</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Support for everything from small balance tweaks to total conversions</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Modding is not an afterthought. It is part of the design.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About the Team</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cyberscape is developed by <strong>AtomicTorch Studio</strong>, an independent team with over a decade of experience building games on Steam. Known for CryoFall and VoidExpanse, the studio focuses on deep, open-ended mechanics, technical robustness, and long-term value and replayability.</p>", "short_description": "Cyberscape is a classic FPS with RPG elements, inspired by the best traditions of the 90s. It features open-ended level design, multiple playstyles, character upgrades, an inventory system, full modding support, and a built-in level editor.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese - Brazil, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Turkish<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3519900/01b2edb4a8e9fa1b1ac21cdb5fb1aba53df83963/header.jpg?t=1777753941", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3519900/fd7c27eecc29f24ffcabcadc7303f14ebf70db2f/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1777753941", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3519900/fd7c27eecc29f24ffcabcadc7303f14ebf70db2f/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1777753941", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> 2 core, 2 GHz<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 2 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Intel HD 4000<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 1 GB available space</li></ul>", "recommended": "<stro